---
// A small centered divider glyph — a mint sprig with a curl of steam,
// tying every section break back to the "salon de thé" concept (the
// client's core product: mint tea). Replaces the previous lotus/petal
// motif inherited from an unrelated Indian-restaurant template — that
// shape carried no meaning for this client. Uses --color-accent (the
// brand's deep green) so it reads as an intentional brand mark rather
// than decoration lifted from elsewhere. Same usage as before: drop it
// between sections wherever a transition deserves a quiet decorative
// beat instead of a flat color change.
---
<div class="flex items-center justify-center py-2" aria-hidden="true">
  <span class="h-px w-10 sm:w-16" style="background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--color-border))"></span>
  <svg width="26" height="22" viewBox="0 0 28 24" fill="none" class="mx-4 shrink-0" style="color: var(--color-accent)">
    <path d="M14 2c-1.2 1-1.6 2-.8 3s1.6 1.6.4 2.6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.1" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.7" />
    <path d="M13 12c-3.2-.4-6-2-7.4-4.6 3.6-1 7 .2 8.8 3 .6 1 .6 2.2-1.4 1.6z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linejoin="round" />
    <path d="M6.4 7.6c2.4 1.4 4.4 2.6 6.2 4.2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.9" stroke-linecap="round" />
    <path d="M15 12c3.2-.4 6-2 7.4-4.6-3.6-1-7 .2-8.8 3-.6 1-.6 2.2 1.4 1.6z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linejoin="round" />
    <path d="M21.6 7.6c-2.4 1.4-4.4 2.6-6.2 4.2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.9" stroke-linecap="round" />
    <path d="M14 12v7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" />
    <circle cx="14" cy="20" r="1" fill="currentColor" />
  </svg>
  <span class="h-px w-10 sm:w-16" style="background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--color-border), transparent)"></span>
</div>
